# Copy to .env and fill in. `.env` is gitignored; this file is not.
#
# The start scripts pass these through to the container with `docker run -e`,
# so nothing here is baked into the image. Set them in your shell instead if
# you prefer — the scripts read the environment first and the file second.
#
# That keeps the key out of the image but not out of the host: `docker
# inspect prelegal` shows it, and so does the container's environment to
# anyone with root or Docker access on that machine. Fine on your own
# machine, not fine on a shared one — use real secret management before
# running this anywhere other people can reach the daemon.

# Lets the AI chat draft the agreement. Get one at https://openrouter.ai/keys.
#
# Optional. Without it the app still runs: the document preview and both
# downloads work as before, and the chat panel alone reports that it is
# unavailable rather than the server refusing to start.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-v1-25a...1e1
